{
  "_comment": "SCENE FILE — the PRE-LOAD screen, page 3 of the intro chain (TegLogo → CeLogo → Loading → Main). Unlike the two logo splashes (single full-bleed sprites on the `splash` behaviour), this is a NATIVE component tree on the `loading` behaviour: a dark backdrop, the sigil zone (reserved — the runtime spinner lands there later), the Septisigil rule, the do-not-close notice, and a `resource_gauge` progress bar. The `loading` behaviour runs the shader-compile phase as a SIMULATED timer for now (`params.seconds`), publishing `loading_progress` (0..1) into the Model each frame; the bar binds it and the pair script (scripts/Loading.lua) derives the percent readout. When the timeline completes the behaviour fires `next` and the `exits` map routes it — that completion is what will ultimately gate the real pre-load. `params.seconds` is the sim duration (the 'longer pause'); a Cancel/Esc backs out via `exit`.",
  "behaviour": "loading",
  "params": {
    "seconds": 6.0
  },
  "exits": {
    "next": {
      "to": "Main",
      "mode": "replace"
    },
    "exit": {
      "to": "Main",
      "mode": "replace"
    }
  },
